Upstream
--------

Wine is developed by the Wine project (https://www.winehq.org/).
Calimocho builds from the official WineHQ source tarball:

    versions.json -> release_engine.wine.url
    versions.json -> release_engine.wine.sha256

(wine-11.20.tar.xz; the same file tree as git tag wine-11.20, commit
7298a818b79446bae153b8d5aa27235ab3703bf9).

Patch 0001 ports the macOS D3DMetal integration from CodeWeavers'
LGPL CrossOver 26.3.0 source drop (https://www.codeweavers.com/crossover/source,
versions.json -> release_engine.cw_donor). The ported files keep
CodeWeavers' copyright notices.

Modifications
-------------

Calimocho does not modify Wine source files in this repository. All
changes are unified-diff patches applied in order from:

    patches/wine-11.20/series

by `tools/release_engine.py build`. Each engine release tag
(engine-11.20-4.0b3-NN) pins the exact patch set that produced that
release.

Corresponding source
--------------------

The complete corresponding source for the LGPL parts of an engine
release is:

    (1) the Wine tarball pinned above, PLUS
    (2) patches/wine-11.20/ and tools/ at the matching engine tag in
        https://github.com/WorkingPrinciple/calimocho, PLUS
    (3) the FreeType, GMP, nettle, libtasn1 and GnuTLS tarballs pinned
        in versions.json -> release_engine.dependency_sources.

Each release ships next to `<engine-id>-source.tar`, which holds all
of these, and `SOURCE.md` inside the engine lists them again.

Written offer (LGPL §6(b))
--------------------------

For at least three (3) years from the date of each engine release, the
Calimocho maintainer offers the complete corresponding source of its
LGPL components to anyone who asks, at no charge beyond the cost of
physically performing the transfer. Ask by opening an issue at:

    https://github.com/WorkingPrinciple/calimocho/issues

with the title "LGPL source request: <engine-id>". This offer is valid
to any third party in possession of the binary.

Other components
----------------

The Apple Game Porting Toolkit components in engine releases
(D3DMetal.framework, libd3dshared.dylib and the Direct3D PE modules)
are governed by Apple's Game Porting Toolkit licence, reproduced at:

    THIRDPARTY/Apple-GPTK/License.rtf

All other bundled components and their licence texts are listed in
LICENSE and shipped under licenses/ in every engine release.
